<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gusiluo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">997–1065</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Gyelsé</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gusiluo was the Tibetan ruler of the Tsongkha kingdom in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amdo">Amdo</a>, around the Huangshui valley of present-day Qinghai. Brought in as a youth around 1008 by Tibetan clans who claimed he descended from the old imperial line, he later set up his own court at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xining">Qingtang</a>, modern Xining. A Buddhist ruler allied with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song dynasty</a>, he controlled trade routes to the west and defeated the Tangut armies of Western Xia in the 1030s.</p></div>
